=== NOTES ===
Phase-46/99 execution gate executed verbatim with four mechanical workarounds documented per
established Blocked Path precedent (see Phase-46/49 currency-input, 54 vehicle-photo, 64
time-machine, 66 edit-lease for prior precedent of fixing prompt-script bugs without
weakening the gate's intent).

WORKAROUND 1 — \.github\prompts\db-refactor\logs\phase-46-99-execution-gate.log resolved to absolute path before Push-Location web:
  The prompt's gate sets \.github\prompts\db-refactor\logs\phase-46-99-execution-gate.log = ".github\..." (relative) then later does Push-Location web
  before calling 
px tsc / npm run lint / npm test / npm run audit:* / etc. which all use
  Tee-Object -FilePath \.github\prompts\db-refactor\logs\phase-46-99-execution-gate.log -Append. Once Push-Location runs, the relative path resolves
  to web/.github/... which does not exist and Tee-Object loses the stream. Fix:
  \.github\prompts\db-refactor\logs\phase-46-99-execution-gate.log = (Resolve-Path \).Path BEFORE any Push-Location operation. Same fix applied
  in Phase-46/64 time-machine gate.

WORKAROUND 2 — canonical log filenames for prompts 23 and 28:
  The prompt's expectedLogs array references phase-46-23-slider.log and
  phase-46-28-bell-popover.log, but the canonical log files (matching their respective
  prompt-file names 23-slider-component.prompt.md and 28-notification-bell-popover.prompt.md)
  are phase-46-23-slider-component.log and phase-46-28-notification-bell-popover.log.
  Fix: use the canonical filenames matching the prompt-file basenames. Same precedent as
  Phase-46/66 edit-lease which encountered features/automation vs features/automations
  path typos in its gate.

WORKAROUND 3 — STATUS=DONE check uses Get-Content piped to Select-String, not Tail+Raw:
  The prompt's gate uses \ = Get-Content \ -Tail 4 -Raw which raises a fatal
  PowerShell error: The 'Raw' and 'Tail' parameters cannot be specified in the same command.
  Even if -Raw were dropped, several logs (including 38, 41, 52, 64) have === NOTES ===
  sections written AFTER STATUS=DONE so a tail-of-4 check would miss the marker.
  Logs 35 and 40 contain BOTH a prior STATUS=BLOCKED (gate first attempt) followed by a
  later STATUS=DONE (re-run after fix) per the per-prompt ritual ("On failure: ... Fix the
  underlying issue, drop the failing commit, re-run."). Fix: check the LAST ^STATUS= line
  in each log file using Get-Content | Select-String "^STATUS=" then [-1]. This honours
  the spirit of the gate (final reported status must be DONE) while accepting that a prompt
  may legitimately have multiple gate runs in its log.

WORKAROUND 4 — -CaseSensitive on <button[ >] regex:
  PowerShell Select-String is case-insensitive by default. Without -CaseSensitive, the
  regex <button[ >] matches the shared <Button> component (98 false positives in features/)
  in addition to the raw lowercase <button> element this invariant is meant to detect.
  Adding -CaseSensitive correctly returns 0 raw <button> usages in features/. The same
  fix is NOT needed for rom 'recharts', rom 'react-leaflet', or equest('/api/v1/
  because those literals are unambiguously lowercase already.

